cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper."
title: "Unrolled Expectation Maximization with Learned Elementwise Extrapolation for Sparse State Space Identification"
type: software
license: GPL-2.0-only
version: "1.0"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of unrolled expectation maximization with a learned elementwise
  extrapolation, a safeguard and a handover to a bounded SQUAREM for estimating sparse transition
  matrices of linear Gaussian state space models, together with the classical baselines (EM,
  SQUAREM, DAAREM, quasi-Newton EM), all simulation scripts of the accompanying paper, a script that
  computes every table and figure of the paper from the raw results, and the figure sources.
keywords:
  - expectation maximization
  - algorithm unrolling
  - learned optimization
  - state space model
  - sparse system identification
  - Kalman smoother
  - extrapolation
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Ruiqi
    affiliation: "Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University"
